eys.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gretchen Whitmer (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open governor's race pits Democrat Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James, with Gretchen Whitmer term-limited. Polling through early October consistently shows Benson ahead, with recent surveys ranging from a 3-point to a 12-point lead and averages clustering near 6 to 8 points. High-quality pollsters like YouGov, NYT/Siena, and Marist all show her in front.\n\nBenson has also more than doubled James's fundraising, holding a large cash advantage heading into the final stretch. Expert raters broadly call the race Lean D, with one Likely D, and prediction markets price Benson's chances around 90-93%. The state's even partisan lean and the open-seat dynamic keep some uncertainty, but the weight of polling, money, and market pricing points to Benson as the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8925, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9071, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9049, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8998, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}]}